    "content": "Watch the 2026 Boston Marathon on April 20 via WCVB (local TV), ESPN2 (national), or streaming on fuboTV and the BAA Racing App. Prime in-person spots include Hopkinton Start, Wellesley \"Scream Tunnel,\" Newton Hills, Heartbreak Hill, or near the Copley Square finish line.Best Places to Watch In-Person (Course Route)Start/Hopkinton (Miles 1-2): High energy, very crowded.Ashland (Miles 3-5): Usually less crowded around Ashland State Park.Natick (Miles 8-11): Family-friendly, crowded at Natick Common.Wellesley (Miles 12-16): Famous \"Scream Tunnel\" near Wellesley College.Newton Hills (Miles 16-21): Challenging for runners, great cheering spots.Heartbreak Hill (Mile 20-21): Intense, iconic, and crowded viewing.Brookline (Miles 23-25): Beacon Street is a great, accessible spot.Finish Line (Mile 26+): Near Copley Square in Boston.Viewing TipsTransportation: Take the MBTA (T-Alerts recommended) as downtown traffic is restricted and street parking is limited.Accessibility: A Sensory-Friendly Zone is available near mile 13.5.Tracking: Use the official B.A.A. Racing App to track runners.TV & Streaming DetailsLocal TV (New England): WCVB Channel 5.National TV: ESPN2.Streaming: fuboTV, Very Local Boston, and ESPN App.",
